  "details": {
    "f66eabaece6e94e0ead680bf460c8299ad4f1565": {
      "message": "feat(context7): add always-on guidance so the tools actually get called\n\nMeasured on this machine (57 sessions, ~5,900 recorded tool calls): the two\nContext7 tools accounted for ~0.3% of calls, and only 2 of 26 sessions reached\nthem organically after install. The MCP client does republish Context7's own\ninitialize.instructions, but that text never names mcp__context7__*; the only\nactionable line nearby points at list_mcp_resources, and Context7 exposes no\nresources.\n\nThe plugin's Host half now registers one prompt section at MCP_SERVERS + 1\n(3101, directly below the vendor paragraph) that names both tools, says they\nbeat memory and web_fetch, and gives the one case that should skip them. It\nself-hides through tools.get() when the connector row is missing or renamed,\ncosts ~90 tokens per request, and turns off with `guidance: false`. Both rows\ngain documented config.\n\nAlso add node:test coverage for placement, gating, renaming and config\nvalidation, plus scripts/usage-report.mjs so \"it never triggers\" can be read\nas a number from committed session logs.",
      "author": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
