    "81cefd61527ae29cd5eab955931620d64992caea": {
      "message": "feat(git): fold the branch sections and move worktrees above remote\n\nThe branches tab now reads local -> worktrees -> remote, and each section folds\nwhen its header is clicked: a repository usually carries more worktrees than\nbranches a reader wants at once, and the worktrees describe this machine while a\nremote branch is just a name.\n\nTwo visual defects of the 0.3.0 panel are fixed with it:\n\n- The primary buttons painted a hard-coded white label on\n  `--dsw-alias-brand-primary`, which is near-white in the dark theme, so the text\n  disappeared and the disabled state read as grey on grey. The label now comes\n  from `--dsw-alias-label-primary-foreground`, the token the host paints on a\n  primary fill, and the disabled state drops the brand fill for a neutral surface\n  with the secondary label.\n- The commit graph drew only the half of a lane below its node: the layout never\n  reported the edge arriving from the row above, so every lane was one dash per\n  commit. That edge is now part of `incoming` — a degenerate curve along the same\n  column — and the lane svg opts out of aspect correction, so filling its row can\n  never scale the drawing away from a seam.",
      "author": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
